To create a fully playable Space Invaders game, you can use the provided `createSpaceInvaders` function. This function takes three parameters:

1. `gameCanvasId` - The ID of the HTML canvas element where the game will be rendered. Make sure you have an HTML canvas element with the specified ID in your HTML document.

2. `width` - The width of the game canvas. The default is 500 pixels.

3. `height` - The height of the game canvas. The default is 500 pixels.

Here's an example of how to use the `createSpaceInvaders` function:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Space Invaders</title>
  <script src="game.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
  <canvas id="gameCanvas" width="500" height="500"></canvas>
  <script>
    createSpaceInvaders('gameCanvas');
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

Make sure to include the `game.js` file that contains the `createSpaceInvaders` function in your HTML document.

The game will start when you call the `createSpaceInvaders` function with the canvas ID as the parameter. The player's ship will appear at the bottom of the canvas, and the enemy invaders will be positioned in formation above the ship.

-controls---
- Move the player's ship left and right using the arrow keys.
- Shoot bullets with the spacebar key.

-objectives---
- The goal is to destroy all the enemy invaders to clear the level.
- If the enemy invaders reach the bottom of the canvas or touch the player's ship, the game will end.

-sprites---
- Player ship (blue)
- Enemy invaders (white)
- Bullets (player: blue, enemy: white)

-score---
- No score system is included in this example code.

-smooth-performance---
The game runs at 60 FPS.

-brownsers-compatibility---
The game should work in all major web browsers, since it does not rely on any external libraries.
